WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:07.830
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this week on
the Flash we met a couple more big comic book

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:12.830
characters and got some more information about
the big villain.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.990
So I’ll start with my top 5 easter eggs
then do my review and circle back around for

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.280
all the other references I spotted.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.600
And hello any new people, if you’re just
finding me for the first time I’m doing

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.200
weekly DC and Marvel videos.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.340
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.970
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.340
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, top 5 easter
eggs,

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.280
Number 5 - Barry Needs Junk Food

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.190
Anyone who saw the original Flash TV Series
with John Wesley Shipp might remember the

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:42.600
scene where he ate like 18 pizzas while Doctor
McGee watched him.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.280
The way Caitlin Snow explained everything
is a lot more complex but The Flash draws

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.519
on the Speed Force to give him his power.

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:52.309
His body is mostly the same, he still has
to burn calories like anyone else.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:53.429
He just burns a shitload more.

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:56.050
That’s where all the junk food comes from.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:05.900
When they went back to Barry’s lab you could
see all the empty pastry boxes.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:12.200
By the end of the episode Cisco had created
a crazy powerful version of a clif bar.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.900
So I don’t think they’ll do a ton more
Junk Food jokes.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.360
We might see him throwing away the occasional
candy bar wrapper though.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.310
One of those energy bars he’s got is the
equivalent of 850 Tacos.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.720
Also equal to one Chipotle Burrito.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.720
Number 4 - We Were All Struck By That Lightning

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.670
This is a huge wink at the comics, at least
one other person in that group was probably

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.230
struck by the speed force lightning.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.210
I won’t say who exactly just in case you
haven’t read the comics.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:45.500
But Caitlin Snow and Cisco Ramon both have
super powers un-related to the lightning.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.360
It’s unclear whether or not the show will
give them powers.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.750
But Caitlin Snow’s alias is Killer Frost,
she has Cold based powers and Cisco’s is

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.670
Vibe, he can create shock waves.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.820
That’s why everytime Danielle Panabaker
makes a funny face when Barry talks about

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:04.600
metahumans I feel like she secretly was affected
by the Star Labs explosion and just isn’t

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.660
telling them.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.599
Number 3 - Metamorpho

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:14.180
Simon Stagg, the person William Sadler was
playing is directly responsible for the creation

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:18.269
of Metamorpho, the show isn’t doing that
character this season, and they just killed

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:24.549
Simon Stagg, but the whole idea of cells adapting
to become anything the body needs is a pretty

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:26.670
good nod.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:32.879
Multiplex is a different villain in the comics,
but his powers are pretty much what you saw.

00:02:32.879 --> 00:02:34.709
He makes copies of himself.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:40.080
It seemed like he died too at the end, so
we might not see him again.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.909
Number 2 - Captain Clone

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:47.489
Cisco naming super villains is probably going
to continue to be a thing which is awesome.

00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:52.700
But Captain Clone is just a wink at Captain
Cold who we’ll meet in Episode 4.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.840
Obviously when we see all the rogues for the
first time they’ll appear their real selves.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.430
So we’ll be meeting Leonard Snart, not Captain
Cold.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.090
He’s being played by Wentworth Miller from
Prison Break.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:06.110
He is probably going to be the coolest villain
this season, no pun intended.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.720
But seriously, he’s not the biggest villain.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.109
If you watched Arrow Season 2, think of him
more as a Brother Blood level villain, like

00:03:14.109 --> 00:03:16.190
a medium bad.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:22.370
and my number 1 easter egg - Firestorm

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.249
Next week is when we’ll meet Ronnie Raymond
aka Firestorm.

00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:29.560
It sounds like it’s going to be a flashback
to before the star labs explosion.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:37.609
He’s Danielle Panabaker’s fiancee, part
of the reason she’s so angry all the time

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:40.959
is because he died, or she thinks he died.

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:44.609
The episode is called “Things You Can’t
Outrun”, which is a reference to the other

00:03:44.609 --> 00:03:49.040
villain they’ll be chasing “Mist”.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.650
I also think it’s a reference to a nuclear
explosion.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.430
Like the flash can’t out run something that
devestating.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:58.470
It’s just a reference to Firestorm’s Nuclear
based powers.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.670
Hopefully we’ll get to see Robbie Amell
as Firestorm in present day.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:06.510
But he’ll eventually be part of Team Flash
the same way Oliver Queen started adding people

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.299
to Team Arrow.

00:04:09.299 --> 00:04:19.949
Very excited, I know all the Tomorrow People
fans were pumped when the cast him as a big

00:04:19.949 --> 00:04:20.949
comic book superhero.

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:23.849
I already did a big explainer video for him
and for captain cold.

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:31.699
So I’ll add links to those in the description
if you want to learn more about those characters.

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:35.940
Just as a bonus WTF Comic Book Moment - Harrison
Wells, we have to talk about him.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:43.580
Clearly someone sinister, if he had been a
future version of Barry he would not have

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:47.400
killed Stagg.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.743
The evidence that he’s really professor
zoom is stacking up.

00:04:49.743 --> 00:04:51.180
There’s still a chance he could be a different
version of the reverse flash.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.340
There are many of them.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.210
I also did a video explaining them all.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.220
Lots of explaining going around.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:59.970
So if you want to dig deeper on all these
huge characters just check the description.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.729
Let me know though, what was your favorite
moment and do you think Harrison Wells is

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:06.110
Professor Zoom or do you think he’s someone
else?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:14.240
Overall I gave the episode an A minus for
digging deeper into the character relationships.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:24.889
All the comic book stuff is great, but that
means nothing if the characters fall flat.

00:05:24.889 --> 00:05:29.401
Of all the relationships on the show, not
sexual relationships, the ones I’m most

00:05:29.401 --> 00:05:34.830
interested in right now are Barry and Caitlin,
Barry and Harrison and Barry and Eddie Thawne.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.110
Eddie Thawne isn’t really much of a character
yet.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:42.659
We’ll probably get a lot more time with
him soon.

00:05:42.659 --> 00:05:46.250
Harrison of course is throwing all the WTF
moments at us, he’s definitely obsessed

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.370
with Barry in a very time travely way.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:53.039
And Caitlin Snow is probably the most complex
character on the show right now.

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:54.620
Which for me, makes her the most interesting.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:06:00.050
She clearly has a lot she’s not telling
everyone.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:03.169
Yet.

00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:11.009
Cisco, Detective West and Iris West are all
totally open books.

00:06:11.009 --> 00:06:15.319
There is nothing they are hiding.

00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:19.280
So most of the intrigue will come from those
other characters.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:24.849
The story was great, Barry realizing his limits
and everyone else realizing that as long as

00:06:24.849 --> 00:06:28.259
Barry Believes in himself, he kind of doesn’t
have limits.

00:06:28.259 --> 00:06:33.169
We’ll continue to learn more about the nature
of the speed force and how his powers work.

00:06:33.169 --> 00:06:36.189
Right now he’s still using it in a relatively
unsophisticated way.

00:06:36.189 --> 00:06:38.940
Like swirling beakers around and running around
things.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:44.080
In the comics, he can vibrate his body so
fast he can pass through solid objects and

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.569
with the aid of the Star Labs jacked up treadmill.

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:48.879
He can travel through time.

00:06:48.879 --> 00:06:52.139
I almost forgot, Treadmill equals cosmic treadmill
easter egg.

00:06:52.139 --> 00:06:56.159
Be sure to let me know if you spotted any
other comic book references in the episode

00:06:56.159 --> 00:06:57.159
that I missed.

00:06:57.159 --> 00:06:58.879
But next week is Firestorm, prepare thyself.

00:06:58.879 --> 00:07:02.360
I’ll post my video after the episode airs.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.030
So be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:09.850
I’ll be posting my Agents of SHIELD video
wednesday morning.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.780
So look out for that too.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:18.040
And Arrow Episode 2 tomorrow night.

